### probe script: p12-final-facts.sh
=== 1. per-user KillUserProcesses (effective, as logind reports it) ===
RuntimePath=/run/user/1000
Service=user@1000.service
Linger=yes
--- the same for the control user (uid 117) ---
RuntimePath=/run/user/117
Service=user@117.service
Linger=no
=== 2. polkit: may THIS caller enable linger for itself? (no --detail; nothing changed) ===
set-self-linger exit=0
Authorization requires authentication and -u wasn't passed.
manage-units exit=2
polkit\56retains_authorization_after_challenge=1
Authorization requires authentication and -u wasn't passed.
set-user-linger exit=2
=== 3. is dbus-broker (the alternative user bus) installed here? ===
ls: cannot access '/usr/lib/systemd/user/dbus-broker.socket': No such file or directory
ls: cannot access '/usr/bin/dbus-broker': No such file or directory
--- which dbus session implementation answers (from the running daemon) ---
    PID CMD
   2342 /usr/bin/dbus-daemon --session --address=systemd: --nofork --nopidfile --systemd-activation --syslog-only
